  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Commit before inference",
      "items": [
        "Successful submit commits the immutable version, approval round, configuration snapshot, evaluation run and audit before provider work.",
        "VLM consumes snapshot attachment bytes; Media and Strategy validate structured outputs against saved policy/rubric and evidence.",
        "AI/provider failure does not roll back a committed submission; it routes an eligible active round to Human Review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Decision and human authority",
      "items": [
        "Decision Policy applies deterministic budget, authority, evidence, confidence and state gates; failed or unknown checks route to HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED.",
        "Runtime engine outcomes are AUTO_APPROVED or HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED. AI auto-reject is unsupported; only the assigned Checker can record REJECTED.",
        "Checker rejection requires a reason. An action that overrides the stored AI recommendation requires an override reason."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Code support vs enabled policy",
      "items": [
        "The code contains a controlled AUTO_APPROVED path; the default unconfigured Auth policy disables it.",
        "Judge Demo seed policy is separate. Auth staging is configuration only and has no approved inference/policy setup.",
        "No live production auto-approval or inference status was verified on 2026-10-17."
      ]
    }
